== Equipment ==

<!-- IMG: Balboan Navy patrol boat — a grey coastal patrol boat with a mounted machine gun on the foredeck cutting through calm blue tropical waters, two naval personnel in white helmets on the bridge wing, a coastline with low hills visible in the background, bright sunlight, professional military photography -->
[[File:Balboan Navy patrol boat.png|thumb|right|300px|A Balboan Navy patrol boat photographed near the Balboa Canal approaches.]]

The BDF's equipment is primarily imported, reflecting Balboa's limited domestic defence industry. Much of the BDF's early equipment consisted of surplus [[Great Adonian War]] materiel donated by coalition forces that had operated from the [[Areza joint military base|Areza military base]] during and after the war. The donated equipment — including small arms, vehicles, vessels, and aircraft — formed the basis of the BDF's inventory through the 1970s and 1980s and was gradually supplemented by purchases from foreign suppliers. In 2001, a comprehensive modernisation programme partially funded by an [[Adonian Community]] loan replaced much of the remaining GAW surplus with modern equipment sourced primarily from manufacturers in [[Balisca]], [[Okaiken]], and [[Volisania]]. The principal foreign suppliers are Balisca, Okaiken, and Volisania, with equipment sourced from each depending on type and requirements. Domestic industry is focused on repair and services, with one domestic manufacturer of small watercraft.

=== Domestic industry ===

The [[Drassanes de Haicang]] is a Balboan shipyard company based at [[Haicang]], [[Estret Province]], that manufactures small watercraft — patrol boats, harbour launches, and coastal patrol vessels — for the BDF Navy and the commercial market. The company also provides ship repair and maintenance services for the Navy and for commercial vessels transiting the [[Balboa Canal]]. The Drassanes de Haicang is the only domestic manufacturer of naval vessels in Balboa; all larger naval vessels are imported from foreign suppliers.

