== Missions and operations ==

=== Primary missions ===

The BDF's primary mission is the defence of the [[Balboa Canal]] and the country's territorial integrity. In practice, the BDF's day-to-day operations are oriented toward domestic security rather than conventional military defence. The Navy's principal role is coast guard duties, including the management of ship traffic in the canal approaches and the country's territorial waters. The Army's principal role is intelligence services, border management, and drug interdiction task forces, with close coordination with civilian police forces. The Air Force provides support to the Army, search and rescue, and reconnaissance.

Balboa's broader defence strategy, however, is based on hosting [[Adonian Community]] coalition forces rather than maintaining a large standing military of its own. The [[Areza joint military base]] and the [[AC Haicang Navy Station]] provide the principal deterrent against external aggression, and the BDF's role is conceived as complementary to the AC presence rather than as a substitute for it. The BDF provides domestic security, canal defence, and support to civilian law enforcement, while the AC coalition forces provide the strategic deterrence that Balboa's small professional force cannot.

The BDF also provides support to civilian law enforcement and to the [[International Cooperative Police Force]] (ICPF) in the event of a security emergency. The BDF and the ICPF operate under separate command structures but coordinate on matters of mutual concern, including canal security and compliance with the [[Twelve Guarantees]].

<!-- IMG: BDF peacekeeping deployment — a small group of Balboan soldiers in blue UN-style helmets standing beside a medical truck in an arid foreign peacekeeping zone, a few dozen personnel, AC flag patch on their shoulders, dusty terrain, documentary war photography style, bright harsh sunlight -->
=== Adonian Community peacekeeping ===

Balboa contributes small deployments — typically a few dozen personnel — to [[Adonian Community]] peacekeeping operations. These deployments have included military observers, medical teams, engineering units, and small infantry detachments. The contributions are modest in scale but represent Balboa's commitment to the AC's collective security framework and its role as a responsible member of the international community.

